  <section>
    <h2>Is StarsJoy an official Telegram partner?</h2>
    <p>No — and answering that honestly is part of what makes a service trustworthy. StarsJoy operates as a reseller of Telegram Stars and Premium, with no official agreement with Telegram. This isn't specific to StarsJoy: Telegram doesn't grant "official partner" status to any third-party bot or site — even TON-based marketplaces like Fragment.com are separate legal entities.</p>
    <p>The problem case is a site that falsely claims to be an "official Telegram representative." StarsJoy makes no such claim: its independent-reseller status isn't hidden, and trust instead comes from verifiable order/review numbers and a clearly stated guarantee.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Are the customer reviews real, not bought?</h2>
    <p>Reviews are published on the <a href="/sharhlar">reviews page</a> with a date — that's the day the customer wrote it, not a moderation date. Any customer can leave a new review after buying; reviews are checked before publishing (to filter spam and off-topic entries), but negative reviews aren't removed.</p>
    <p>The simplest way to check: open the page and look at the spread of dates and writing style — dozens of reviews written on the same day in the same style would signal fake volume. StarsJoy's reviews instead arrive spread out over months.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Is there a money-back guarantee?</h2>
